## display Core String Utilities
##
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).
## FFI string ownership helpers.

## Returns a private heap copy of s.
##
## Native FFI `str` results are zero-copy views into C static buffers: the
## bytes change under us when the same native function runs again (e.g. a
## second `display_at()` call overwrites the first entry text). String
## operations (concat, slicing) pin heap copies, so route every stored or
## returned FFI string through this helper at the module boundary.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `s`: Source string (possibly an FFI view).
##
## ### Returns
## Private copy safe to hold across further FFI calls.
pub function str_owned(s: string) -> string
    return "" + s
end
